    <string name="tutorial_title">Get and set up an API key</string>
    <string name="tutorial_intro">This app uses the free OpenWeatherMap API to display the weather. Follow these steps to get a key and configure it.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_step1_title">1. Create an OpenWeatherMap account</string>
    <string name="tutorial_step1_text">Go to openweathermap.org and create a free account (Sign In → Create an Account). Confirm your e-mail address via the link you receive.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_step2_title">2. Open the API keys page</string>
    <string name="tutorial_step2_text">Once signed in, open your username at the top right then \u201cMy API keys\u201d, or go directly to the home.openweathermap.org/api_keys page.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_step3_title">3. Generate the key</string>
    <string name="tutorial_step3_text">On the \u201cMy API keys\u201d page, a key is generated automatically (Default). You can also create a new one with a name. Copy the 32-character string.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_step4_title">4. Wait for activation</string>
    <string name="tutorial_step4_text">A new key can take up to a few hours (often 10 to 120 minutes) to activate. Until it does, the API returns \u201cInvalid API key\u201d.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_step5_title">5. Enter the key in the app</string>
    <string name="tutorial_step5_text">In the app, open the menu (three dots at the top right) → \u201cAPI key\u201d, paste the key then tap \u201cSave\u201d. The key is stored on the device.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_step6_title">6. Check the free plan</string>
    <string name="tutorial_step6_text">The \u201cFree\u201d plan (Current Weather, Forecast 5 days/3h, Geocoding) is enough for the app. One Call API 3.0 is not used here. Your free 60 calls/min cover personal use.</string>
